Z||000025||cardealer||04-13-2001||01:18 AM||||pretty much my own "kit". i purchased an old zulmat adaptor plate and front motor mount off ebay and used them for templates to create something that would work for me. and then resold the zulmat stuff for what i paid for them. you would just die if you if you really knew how little of expense i had on this project! by no means my setup will ever surpass the other kits on the market but it is different in design in many ways. not better just different. unless you have countless resources involving the design and fabrication of pieces please dont attempt this on your own. from what i can tell from my own research you just cant beat the archie kit. although this wasnt that hard of a project, and only took me 5 full days to do the removal and installation i know i will never do another v8 fiero project without using a archie kit. beat me, slam me, what ever.... in my opinon. it is still the best option on the market. i have never meet or even spoken to archie (not counting here on this forum (thanks for all the advice you give everyone archie)) but i just like his simplicity of design, as all most anyone could accomplish a swap with his kit and service. i did what i wanted to do, my own setup, now if, (BIG IF),i do it again i want to focus on elements of engine design and leave all the other stuff to archie. i already got a big block s10 blazer swap in mind soon !! ||||reg||1
Z||000026||danny boy||04-13-2001||01:47 AM|||| I'm running a holley 750 dbl pmpr Mech. secondaries on my Nova with a built 355SBC.loads up trying to idle,uses a whole lot of gas but anything smaller and it loses ass. Besides,werent 750cfm Qjets factory on GM SBC cars in days of old?||||reg||1
